Roast.pet Weird Builder Projects =E2=80=94 RETRY of previously failed 11:24=
 run

3 useful new finds after screening 25+ candidates and deduplicating
prior discoveries.

1) Vikhas/pet-segmentation =E2=80=94 BENCHMARK / COPY MECHANISM
Zero-star, seven-commit pet-specific matting project with lightweight
MODNet and a higher-detail U-Net =E2=86=92 dynamic trimap =E2=86=92 FBA ref=
inement
path. Pet-domain adaptation uses pseudo-labels and Laplacian-pyramid
loss intended to retain fur detail. Reported Oxford-IIIT Pet test
Dice: MODNet 0.8290; FBA 0.8462. Provides weights, evaluation code,
batch inference and Flask comparison UI. No clear permissive license
was established, so do not ship code/weights until provenance is
resolved.
Experiment: benchmark against current matting stack on 100 difficult
customer-style pet images and measure manual-correction rate.

2) aserper/etsy-mcp =E2=80=94 REUSE NOW
Seven-star, 21-commit MIT Etsy MCP exposing 37 tools covering roughly
70 Etsy API endpoints: draft/update/delete listings, images, listing
video, inventory, taxonomy, shipping profiles, receipts/orders,
shipment creation, reviews, payments/ledger and return policies.
Handles OAuth2 PKCE, token refresh, concurrency-safe rate limiting,
exponential backoff and OpenAPI-generated TypeScript types.
Experiment: disposable draft =E2=86=92 create =E2=86=92 thumbnail =E2=86=92=
 listing video =E2=86=92
inventory =E2=86=92 readback =E2=86=92 retry exercise. If it passes, avoid =
building a
low-level Etsy client.

3) hmns-webAR =E2=80=94 COPY RECORD/SHARE MECHANISM
Small MindAR/Three.js project notable for including screenshot/video
recording and sharing as part of the AR experience.
Roast.pet loop to test: scan card =E2=86=92 pet appears/roasts =E2=86=92 re=
cord =E2=86=92 share.
Experiment on iPhone Safari and Android Chrome for audio inclusion,
resolution, orientation, target-loss behavior and native sharing.
Verify repository license before copying implementation.

TOP 5 THINGS NOT TO BUILD OURSELVES
1. Etsy OAuth/token/rate-limit/retry infrastructure.
2. Etsy listing-video and ordinary listing/order wrappers.
3. Pet-specific fur-matting research before benchmarking existing
pet-trained work.
4. Another WebAR tracking framework.
5. AR screenshot/record/share plumbing before testing an existing
implementation.

Most surprising: Vikhas/pet-segmentation.
Fastest integration win: aserper/etsy-mcp.
Repo/author worth following: aserper/etsy-mcp.

Architecture note: commerce should remain a replaceable adapter;
Roast.pet should concentrate proprietary work on pet identity,
comedy/performance, QA and accumulated order/feedback data.
